WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.480
1989, Creil. Three girls are excluded from
their «collège» for wearing headscarves.

2
00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:11.240
The «Conseil d'État» says
religious signs are not,

3
00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:14.930
in themselves, incompatible
with «la laïcité».

4
00:00:14.930 --> 00:00:19.590
Then, in 2004, a law bans
conspicuous religious signs

5
00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:21.850
for pupils in state schools.

6
00:00:21.850 --> 00:00:25.850
The Constitution calls France
«une République indivisible,

7
00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:28.450
laïque, démocratique et sociale».

8
00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:30.820
So why can't pupils wear a headscarf,

9
00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:33.190
when university students can?

10
00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:36.610
In this mission, you'll build
a timeline of «la laïcité»,

11
00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:40.290
from 1789 to 2023.

12
00:00:40.290 --> 00:00:42.040
Then you'll sort a teacher,

13
00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:46.060
a parent, a patient and a
pupil into three columns,

14
00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:48.150
and argue both readings.

15
00:00:48.150 --> 00:00:51.170
Your mission: work out
where the rule stops,

16
00:00:51.170 --> 00:00:52.350
and explain why.
